  "description": "Bounded integer by rejection sampling (not modulo): threshold = 2^64 mod bound; draw from the stream until a draw >= threshold; the result is that draw mod bound. The stream from a state is draw k = splitmix64(state + (k-1) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15), k = 1, 2, ... bound is from 1 to 2^64-1. PROVISIONAL until F1.1: the scheduler owns the exact function and may amend this file; it is published here so the numbers are checked once. Every 64-bit value is an object: dec (unsigned decimal string), hex (16 lower-case digits, no prefix), hi and lo (its high and low 32 bits as 8 lower-case hex digits), so a port without a native 64-bit integer can check each step.",
